laurel 2201: Mi A3 AMOLED brightness and panel power: panel from the INTF_1 timing, DCS max 2047 (Samsung s6e8fco) / 4095 (GVO r692a9), AppleARMBacklight on by default with the apollo 0154 slider protocol, fades (apollo 0151). The Mi A3 has two AMOLEDs (laurel_sprout-trinket-display.dtsi): Samsung bl-max 2047, GVO bl-max 4095, both min 4, default 268, DCS 0x51 MSB first (F9S dsi_panel_set_brightness), 0x53 0x20 brightness control on. ABL/Mu leave the video timing in INTF_1 HSYNC_CTL: htotal 1404 / pulse 40 = Samsung, 1360 / 136 = GVO; unknown = Samsung range. Self-check at start: the DT default level through the DSI command DMA; no DONE = feature off (no backlight service, display off keeps the black frame). AppleARMBacklight (topaz 0105, opt-in since topaz 0110) is published by default: IODisplayParameters brightness {0, 255, value} + brightness-nits + max-nits 430; CoreBrightness's {brightness, FadePeriod} (apollo 0154: DBV = max * (v/255)^2) and the topaz brightness-nits / IOMFBBrightnessLevel (nits 16.16, linear to DBV) both work. blWork walks to a new level in 16 ms steps over the fade time. Display off: fade the light out over 300 ms, DBV 0, 0x28, 20 ms, 0x10, 120 ms; on: 0x11, 120 ms, 0x29, 0x53 0x20, one frame, fade in to the last non-zero level. dsiSend sets COMMAND_MODE_DMA_CTRL bit 28 (embedded mode) as Linux does. Line: `LAUREL BACKLIGHT: on: DCS max N (<panel>: INTF1 hsync 0x...), level 268, 430 nits, fade 300 ms, AppleARMBacklight published`. Kill switches: sweetbl=0 (no backlight service), laurelfade=0 (no fades), sweetfb_stayon=1 (topaz: ignore display off).

